            <title>[LU-21029] sanity-lfsck test_38: (2) only 0 of 4 MDTs are in completed (layout LFSCK stays partial)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21029</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-lfsck test_38 (DNE, 4 MDTs, 4 OSTs, ldiskfs, el9.7 servers) fails at sanity-lfsck.sh:6064, the layout wait after the foreign-file namespace pass:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;(2) only 0 of 4 MDTs are in completed&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The namespace LFSCK -A -r completed on all MDTs. The following "lfsck_start -t layout -A -r" then left all 4 MDTs with lfsck_query layout_mdts_partial: 4 and mdd.*.lfsck_layout "status: partial" for the whole 600 s wait, while every OST's lfsck_layout was "completed" and oi_scrub completed everywhere. No errors in the MDS or OSS dmesg. The test creates only a foreign-layout file (no data I/O).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same error text has hit sanity-lfsck test_33 on 5 other changes in the last 30 days (68436, 68420, 69717, 68415, 65094 PS45), under EX-14175; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19842" title="sanity-lfsck: test_33 Error: (2) only of 4 MDTs are in completed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19842"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19842&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (awk quoting) and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20263" title="sanity-lfsck test_33: Error: '(2) only of 1 MDTs are in completed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20263"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20263&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (lfsck_stop -A in test_32b) are resolved and their fixes are in this tree (master 31be13da3c22), so they do not cover it. Retests of those sessions passed (e.g. 68415 PS30), so it is intermittent, about 0.1 to 0.2 percent of sanity-lfsck runs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not caused by Change 65094 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19895" title="implement large folio support" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19895"&gt;LU-19895&lt;/a&gt;, client-side folio changes, nothing touches lfsck or the servers' lfsck code).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-65094-ps46-016ff42a4654 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/65094" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/65094&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
